Hierarchical Inheritance

Definition

    Hierarchical inheritance is a type of inheritance in which multiple child classes inherit from a single parent class.

    One superclass is shared by many subclasses.

          Vehicle
         /   |   \
      Car  Bike Truck

    Every child inherits the common properties of Vehicle.


    A Vehicle has common properties like:

        start()
        stop()

    Different vehicles have their own behaviors.

        Car → drive()
        Bike → ride()
        Truck → loadGoods()